// Package queryplanner turns a Brief + known entities + date ranges into
// provider-agnostic query plans with per-query provenance. It is extracted
// from throughline's app/acquire/planner.go and generalized for reuse.
//
// # Two-phase planning
//
// Phase 1 (deterministic): keyword extraction from the brief text and
// entity-email expansion produce provider-specific query strings without any
// LLM call. This phase always runs and always produces useful results.
//
// Phase 2 (optional LLM refinement): if a Refiner is supplied, it may
// suggest additional queries. LLM refinement degrades gracefully — errors
// return the deterministic queries unchanged. The Refiner is a caller-supplied
// interface; this package imports no llmclient, keeping layering clean.
//
// # DLP warnings
//
// Each query string is scanned for raw PII patterns (SSN, phone number) via
// a caller-supplied ScreenFunc. Warnings are attached to the PlannedQuery.
// The screen function is optional; pass nil to skip DLP scanning.
//
// # Provenance
//
// Deterministic queries are tagged IsAI=false; LLM-refined queries are tagged
// IsAI=true. The rationale field explains why each query was generated.
//
// # Concurrency contract
//
// Planner is safe for concurrent use after construction. All fields are
// read-only after NewPlanner returns. The injected ScreenFunc and Refiner must
// also be safe for concurrent use if the Planner is used concurrently.
//
// CUE contracts live in schema.cue; this file and queryplanner.go are the Go
// counterpart and must stay in sync.
package queryplanner

import (
	"context"
	"time"
)

// Brief is the human-authored description of what the investigator seeks.
type Brief struct {
	// ID uniquely identifies this brief.
	ID string
	// Text is the free-text investigation description.
	Text string
}

// EntityInfo is a known participant or entity whose contact details are used
// to generate targeted email/document search queries.
type EntityInfo struct {
	// DisplayName is the entity's human-readable name (used for document searches).
	DisplayName string
	// Emails is the list of known email addresses for this entity.
	Emails []string
	// Aliases are additional identifiers (email-like values are extracted
	// automatically; non-email aliases are ignored by the email expansion).
	Aliases []string
}

// DateRange bounds the search period. Zero-value fields mean unbounded.
type DateRange struct {
	// Start is the inclusive lower bound (zero = no lower bound).
	Start time.Time
	// End is the exclusive upper bound (zero = no upper bound).
	End time.Time
}

// PlannedQuery is a single search query targeting one provider.
type PlannedQuery struct {
	// Provider identifies the search provider (e.g. "gmail", "drive").
	Provider string
	// Account is the specific provider account to query. May be empty when
	// the caller supplies a single-account default at execution time.
	Account string
	// Query is the provider-native query string.
	Query string
	// Rationale explains why this query is expected to produce relevant results.
	Rationale string
	// IsAI is true when the query was generated by an LLM (Phase 2). False
	// for deterministic queries generated by Phase 1 logic.
	IsAI bool
	// Warnings is a list of DLP-related cautions about the query string.
	// Empty when no warnings apply.
	Warnings []string
}

// ScreenFunc inspects a query string for DLP concerns and returns a slice of
// warning messages (empty = clean). The function must be safe for concurrent
// use when the Planner is used concurrently. Pass nil to disable screening.
type ScreenFunc func(query string) []string

// RefinedQuery is one query item returned by the Refiner.
type RefinedQuery struct {
	// Provider is the target provider for this query (e.g. "gmail", "drive").
	// If empty, the Planner uses a default provider ("gmail").
	Provider string
	// Query is the provider-native query string.
	Query string
	// Rationale explains why the LLM suggested this query.
	Rationale string
}

// Refiner is the optional LLM refinement seam. Implementors call the LLM,
// parse its JSON output, and return suggested additional queries. On any
// error, return nil (the Planner degrades to deterministic-only).
//
// The Planner passes a summary of the brief and existing queries so the
// Refiner can avoid proposing duplicates. The returned queries are appended
// to the deterministic set and tagged IsAI=true.
//
// The Refiner must be safe for concurrent use if the Planner is used
// concurrently. The Planner never calls Refiner in parallel with itself for
// a single Plan call; concurrent callers each get their own Refine invocation.
type Refiner interface {
	// Refine takes the brief text and a summary of existing queries and
	// returns additional suggested queries. Return nil on any error or when
	// no additional queries are warranted.
	Refine(ctx context.Context, briefText string, existingQueries []string) []RefinedQuery
}
